.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-MACHINE-SHARE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-machine-share - Share your personal machine with a team; grants are separate. A team that approves new machines holds it until an owner or admin accepts it


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team machine share <team> <machine-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Share your personal machine with the team. You keep ownership; sharing alone lets nobody
use the machine, so add a grant with pb team machine grant. If the team requires approval for
new machines (pb team machine approval), the machine waits until an owner or admin accepts it.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for share

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team machine share acme m_abc123 --generation 9
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-machine(1)\fP
